 27	/**
 28	 * Agent-side implementation of the ACP (Agent Client Protocol) session that manages
 29	 * bidirectional JSON-RPC communication between agents and clients. This is the agent-side
 30	 * counterpart to {@link AcpClientSession}.
 31	 *
 32	 * <p>
 33	 * The session manages:
 34	 * <ul>
 35	 * <li>Request/response handling with unique message IDs</li>
 36	 * <li>Notification processing</li>
 37	 * <li>Message timeout management</li>
 38	 * <li>Transport layer abstraction</li>
 39	 * <li>Single-turn enforcement (only one prompt active at a time per session; a turn ends
 40	 * with its prompt's response, also after {@code session/cancel})</li>
 41	 * </ul>
 42	 *
 43	 * <p>
 44	 * This is the agent-side session that receives requests from clients (initialize,
 45	 * newSession, prompt, etc.) and sends requests to clients (readTextFile, writeTextFile,
 46	 * requestPermission, etc.)
 47	 * </p>
